') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 1, 'failure', '`Error: Permission denied (os error 13)` — compute_ctl, nothing else', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','`Error: Permission denied (os error 13)` — compute_ctl, nothing else']::text[], 6, 20, '## `Error: Permission denied (os error 13)` — compute_ctl, nothing else

```
INFO compute build_tag: release-compute-9073
Error: Permission denied (os error 13)
```

The container restarts forever; no file is named. compute_ctl could not READ
its spec/config file. The compute container runs as `postgres` uid 1000, so
a root-owned `0600` spec — the natural result of rendering it with
root''s umask — is invisible to it. Fix: `chown 1000:1000`, mode `0400`, and
enforce that on *every* path that touches the file: the converge render, the
unchanged branch of the render, rotation, and rotation''s rollback. (The
rollback restoring a root-owned backup is how this was hit the second time.)

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 2, 'failure', '`File exists (os error 17)` + missing postgresql.conf', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','`File exists (os error 17)` + missing postgresql.conf']::text[], 21, 33, '## `File exists (os error 17)` + missing postgresql.conf

```
ERROR could not start the compute node: File exists (os error 17)
PG:postgres: could not access the server configuration file
  "/var/db/postgres/compute/postgresql.conf": No such file or directory
```

A volume (or any pre-existing directory) sits on the pgdata path. compute_ctl
insists on creating pgdata itself; a root-owned mountpoint there fails the
boot. Remove the volume — compute local state is a disposable projection of
the storage tier, and mounting it buys nothing.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 3, 'failure', '`FATAL: lock file "/tmp/.s.PGSQL.55433.lock" already exists`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','`FATAL: lock file "/tmp/.s.PGSQL.55433.lock" already exists`']::text[], 34, 48, '## `FATAL: lock file "/tmp/.s.PGSQL.55433.lock" already exists`

```
FATAL:  lock file "/tmp/.s.PGSQL.55433.lock" already exists
HINT:  Is another postmaster (PID 22) using socket file "/tmp/.s.PGSQL.55433"?
ERROR could not start the compute node: Postgres exited unexpectedly with code 1
```

After a container stop/start (or host reboot with `restart: unless-stopped`):
the writable layer keeps `/tmp`, the stale lock survives, and every
subsequent boot dies while compute_ctl loops init→failed. Two-part fix:
mount a **tmpfs on `/tmp`** so unattended restarts survive, and treat the
container as **recreate-only** (`docker compose up -d --force-recreate
compute`) — which is required anyway for spec changes to apply.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 4, 'failure', 'Pageserver: `Failed to create tenants root dir … Permission denied`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','Pageserver: `Failed to create tenants root dir … Permission denied`']::text[], 49, 59, '## Pageserver: `Failed to create tenants root dir … Permission denied`

```
Error: Failed to create tenants root dir at ''/data/.neon/tenants''
Caused by: Permission denied (os error 13)
```

The storage image runs as `neon` uid 1000; a root-owned bind mount on
`/data/.neon/` blocks it. `chown 1000:1000` the host directory (and the
`pageserver.toml`/`identity.toml` you place inside it).

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 5, 'failure', '`Cannot run timeline checkpoint because pageserver was compiled without testing APIs`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','`Cannot run timeline checkpoint because pageserver was compiled without testing APIs`']::text[], 60, 71, '## `Cannot run timeline checkpoint because pageserver was compiled without testing APIs`

```
{"msg":"\"Cannot run timeline checkpoint because pageserver was compiled without testing APIs\""}
```

`PUT /v1/tenant/{t}/timeline/{tl}/checkpoint` is a testing-build feature;
release images do not have it. To force WAL to R2, close a segment with
`SELECT pg_switch_wal();` (superuser) — the safekeeper offloads closed
segments within seconds. Layer uploads cannot be forced at all on release
images; they follow the pageserver''s checkpoint cadence.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 6, 'failure', 'rclone → R2: `AccessDenied` on writes the token should allow', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','rclone → R2: `AccessDenied` on writes the token should allow']::text[], 72, 84, '## rclone → R2: `AccessDenied` on writes the token should allow

```
ERROR : .colors-init: Failed to copy: AccessDenied: Access Denied
	status code: 403, request id: , host id:
```

Reads work, tofu writes the same bucket with the same keys — but rclone
fails every upload. Old rclone (Ubuntu 24.04''s 1.60) precedes the first
upload with a bucket check/create, and `CreateBucket` is denied for a
bucket-scoped R2 token; the surfaced error looks like a plain write denial.
Fix: `RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_NO_CHECK_BUCKET=true`.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 7, 'failure', 'rclone → R2: `NotImplemented: Not Implemented status code: 501`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','rclone → R2: `NotImplemented: Not Implemented status code: 501`']::text[], 85, 95, '## rclone → R2: `NotImplemented: Not Implemented status code: 501`

`rclone rcat` (unknown-size streaming upload) is a 501 against R2 on this
rclone vintage, and `copyto` trips a 501 on its first attempt''s post-upload
verification. Fix: never `rcat` — stage a known-size tmpfile and `copyto` —
plus `RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_NO_HEAD=true`. Configure rclone entirely from env
(`RCLONE_CONFIG_R2_TYPE=s3`, `PROVIDER=Cloudflare`, keys, `ENDPOINT`,
`REGION=auto`): no config file to manage or leak. Both rclone entries are
vintage-bound — see the retest conditions in `pins.md` before carrying the
flags onto a newer rclone.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 8, 'failure', '`remote_consistent_lsn` is `0/0` — and it is not (necessarily) broken', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','`remote_consistent_lsn` is `0/0` — and it is not (necessarily) broken']::text[], 96, 104, '## `remote_consistent_lsn` is `0/0` — and it is not (necessarily) broken

Right after a pageserver restart or a fresh generation attach the metric
reads `0/0` even when R2 holds a complete, recoverable copy; it was observed
advancing (`0/0 → 0/8006A48`) only while the process ran. Never gate a
converge or a health check on it post-restart. Conversely, do not let an old
object satisfy an upload-health gate: require a NEW safekeeper segment
beyond a pre-`pg_switch_wal` listing baseline.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 9, 'failure', 'Ansible: `failed at splitting arguments, either an unbalanced jinja2 block or quotes`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','Ansible: `failed at splitting arguments, either an unbalanced jinja2 block or quotes`']::text[], 105, 111, '## Ansible: `failed at splitting arguments, either an unbalanced jinja2 block or quotes`

A `shell:` block task that is valid bash still fails to load when the block
contains an **odd number of apostrophes — in a comment**
(`# the container''s postgres user`). Ansible''s splitter counts quotes across
the whole block. Keep task comments apostrophe-free.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 10, 'failure', 'The `ssh -f` tunnel that dies exactly when you use it', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','The `ssh -f` tunnel that dies exactly when you use it']::text[], 112, 122, '## The `ssh -f` tunnel that dies exactly when you use it

An acceptance probe: `ssh -f -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes -L port:… host
sleep 45` "succeeds", then psql gets `Connection refused` — and the step
took suspiciously close to 45s. The daemonized ssh child inherits the
runner''s stdout/stderr pipes; any runner that waits for the streams to close
blocks until the remote `sleep` exits, then proceeds against a dead tunnel.
Fix: wrap in `bash -c ''… >/dev/null 2>&1''` so the child holds /dev/null.
Related: psql `-tAc` with multiple statements prints command tags
(`INSERT 0 1`) before the value — parse the last line.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 11, 'failure', 'Ubuntu 24.04: `No package matching ''awscli'' is available`', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','Ubuntu 24.04: `No package matching ''awscli'' is available`']::text[], 123, 128, '## Ubuntu 24.04: `No package matching ''awscli'' is available`

Verified only this far: `apt` on the Vultr Ubuntu 24.04 image (os id 2284)
resolves no `awscli` package at all. Use rclone (see above) or ship the AWS
CLI yourself.

') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.section (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, kind, heading, heading_path, start_line, end_line, body) VALUES ('neon-single-node', '7aa2034b2b3aa012feb01c55278f7d03f1af6856045758aec01b14ef5a0f4066', 'references/failure-catalogue.md', 12, 'failure', 'A 0-byte ownership marker', ARRAY['Failure catalogue','A 0-byte ownership marker']::text[], 129, 136, '## A 0-byte ownership marker

An empty object satisfies `existence` checks forever while carrying no
ownership — and `rclone cat` on it exits 0, so a guard like
`if ! rclone cat …` never rewrites it. Treat emptiness as absence, verify
every marker write by read-back, and persist the generation counter *before*
the attach it covers (an interruption then burns a number instead of handing
a later recovery a stale generation).
') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
