iners are both up, docker compose ps says everything is running. what am i missing?", "expected_output": "Should identify the capture -> Kafka -> plugin-server -> ClickHouse chain, and diagnose plugin-server silent-exit causes correctly. Must NOT advise unsetting PLUGIN_SERVER_MODE, which causes a zero exit rather than an all-capability server.", "files": [], "assertions": ["Identifies the capture -> Kafka -> plugin-server -> ClickHouse ingestion chain", "States that a 200 from /capture/ only proves the event reached capture, not storage", "States that an unset PLUGIN_SERVER_MODE causes a clean zero exit rather than a default all-capability server", "Does NOT advise unsetting PLUGIN_SERVER_MODE or PLUGIN_SERVER_CAPABILITIES as a fix", "Names a plugin-server failure that is only visible after raising the log level above info", "Names at least two of: GeoIP database missing, Redis clients falling back to loopback, ENCRYPTION_SALT_KEYS unset, application/plugin-server commit mismatch", "Warns that ''docker compose ps running'' is not evidence a process is working"]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.eval_case (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, source_id, name, prompt, expected_output, assertions, raw_case) VALUES ('posthog-single-node', 'fbc57a791e955757d0d879006695cc264b23ad16435535826178bad3653a0832', 'evals/evals.json', 2, '2', 'converge-playbook-ordering', 'i need an ansible playbook that takes a fresh ubuntu 24.04 box and brings up a single-node posthog with docker compose, including running all the migrations so the thing is actually usable at the end. it needs to be idempotent - i''ll be running it repeatedly as i iterate on the config. assume the compose file and clickhouse configs already exist as templates i''ll be copying over', 'Playbook starting datastores only before migrating, SYSTEM FLUSH LOGS before migrate_clickhouse, migrate with the application down, container recreation keyed on what the server actually loaded rather than Ansible change flags, async migration handling to unblock Celery, and a long health-gate timeout.', '["Starts the datastores before the application rather than the whole stack at once", "Runs manage.py migrate with the application container down", "Runs SYSTEM FLUSH LOGS before migrate_clickhouse", "Keys container recreation on state observed from the server, not Ansible change flags", "Handles async migrations so Celery can start", "Sets a health-gate timeout substantially longer than five minutes", "Playbook parses as valid YAML"]', '{"id": 2, "name": "converge-playbook-ordering", "prompt": "i need an ansible playbook that takes a fresh ubuntu 24.04 box and brings up a single-node posthog with docker compose, including running all the migrations so the thing is actually usable at the end. it needs to be idempotent - i''ll be running it repeatedly as i iterate on the config. assume the compose file and clickhouse configs already exist as templates i''ll be copying over", "expected_output": "Playbook starting datastores only before migrating, SYSTEM FLUSH LOGS before migrate_clickhouse, migrate with the application down, container recreation keyed on what the server actually loaded rather than Ansible change flags, async migration handling to unblock Celery, and a long health-gate timeout.", "files": [], "assertions": ["Starts the datastores before the application rather than the whole stack at once", "Runs manage.py migrate with the application container down", "Runs SYSTEM FLUSH LOGS before migrate_clickhouse", "Keys container recreation on state observed from the server, not Ansible change flags", "Handles async migrations so Celery can start", "Sets a health-gate timeout substantially longer than five minutes", "Playbook parses as valid YAML"]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO catalog.eval_case (skill_slug, version_id, path, ordinal, source_id, name, prompt, expected_output, assertions, raw_case) VALUES ('posthog-single-node', 'fbc57a791e955757d0d879006695cc264b23ad16435535826178bad3653a0832', 'evals/evals.json', 3, '3', 'pin-bump', 'our self-hosted posthog has been pinned to the same posthog/posthog image since last august and i want to move it forward to something current before we onboard another team onto it. it''s working fine right now which is exactly why i''m nervous. what do i actually need to be careful about here, and what''s the order of operations?', 'Should require the application and plugin server to move to one shared commit, check the ClickHouse version upstream pins, re-resolve the capture digest, regenerate the schema checkpoint, and re-verify end to end rather than trusting a health endpoint.', '["Requires the application and plugin server to move to the same commit", "Says to check which ClickHouse version upstream pins at the target commit", "Says to re-resolve the capture image digest because its tag moves", "Says a schema checkpoint from a different commit must be regenerated or will be refused", "Warns about a schema/consumer column mismatch of the posthog_person.last_seen_at kind", "Requires end-to-end event verification rather than trusting a health endpoint", "Gives an explicit order of operations"]', '{"id": 3, "name": "pin-bump", "prompt": "our self-hosted posthog has been pinned to the same posthog/posthog image since last august and i want to move it forward to something current before we onboard another team onto it. it''s working fine right now which is exactly why i''m nervous. what do i actually need to be careful about here, and what''s the order of operations?", "expected_output": "Should require the application and plugin server to move to one shared commit, check the ClickHouse version upstream pins, re-resolve the capture digest, regenerate the schema checkpoint, and re-verify end to end rather than trusting a health endpoint.", "files": [], "assertions": ["Requires the application and plugin server to move to the same commit", "Says to check which ClickHouse version upstream pins at the target commit", "Says to re-resolve the capture image digest because its tag moves", "Says a schema checkpoint from a different commit must be regenerated or will be refused", "Warns about a schema/consumer column mismatch of the posthog_person.last_seen_at kind", "Requires end-to-end event verification rather than trusting a health endpoint", "Gives an explicit order of operations"]}') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
